t-tool_help-voc = Record the customer's statements, group them into needs and break them down into drivers and measurable CTQs, with unit and limits.
t-tool_help-sipoc = Suppliers, inputs, the process in 5 to 7 steps, outputs and customers, from left to right.
t-tool_help-pareto = Sorts the categories, shows the cumulative percentage and highlights the vital few, which add up to 80 %.
t-tool_help-data_collection = For each measure: what it is, how to measure it (operational definition), the sampling and who collects.
t-tool_help-ishikawa = The effect at the head and the causes by category (6Ms). Mark each cause as probable, verified or ruled out, with the evidence.
t-tool_help-five_whys = Ask "why?" starting from the problem, with evidence at each level; a why can have more than one branch.
t-tool_help-cause_effect = Weigh the outputs by the customer and give each input 0, 1, 3 or 9 per output; the total ranks the inputs for the analysis.
t-tool_help-fmea = For each failure mode: S, O and D from 1 to 10, the RPN and the action priority. The recommended action becomes a card on the board.
t-tool_help-control_plan = How each characteristic stays under control after the project. Every critical characteristic of the FMEA needs a line.
t-tool_help-response_plan = For each signal (chart rule, limit, alarm): the immediate action, the containment and who to call. The signal opens a card.
t-tool_help-a3 = One page with the whole project, built from the other deliverables; add the team's notes.
t-tool_help-vsm = Each process with its cycle time, availability and the inventory before it; with the demand, the app calculates the takt, the lead time ladder and the cycle efficiency. The future state comes out of the current state.
t-tool_help-selection = Compare solutions or concepts by weighted criteria: in the weighted matrix each option gets 1 to 5; in the Pugh matrix, better (+), same (S) or worse (−) than the reference. Impact and effort build the priority grid.
t-tool_help-five_s = The checklist by sense and the area audits, each question scored from 0 to 4. The app adds up by sense, shows the radar of the last audit and the trend.
t-tool_help-smed = Each changeover activity with its time and class: internal (machine stopped) or external (machine running). Say what each one becomes after the study; the setup time is the sum of the internal ones.
t-tool_help-standard_work = Each operator's elements with manual, automatic and walking times. With the takt, the app builds the combination table, the balancing and the minimum number of operators.
t-tool_help-kaizen_event = The preparation, the agenda for the 3 to 5 days, the open items (which go to the action board) and the follow-up at 30, 60 and 90 days.
t-tool_help-pdca = Each cycle records the hypothesis, what was done, what was checked and what was standardised or adjusted. The next cycle starts from what the previous one learned.
